Rule 1 (input matrix must be at least 2-dimensional and square in its last two dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 2 ∧ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) = shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 2)
>>
Rule 2 (input matrix must have a floating-point or complex data type)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≥ 6 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 10
>>
Rule 3 (the square dimensions of the input matrix must be at least 1)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 2 ∧ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) ≥ 1
>>
Rule 4 (output mode must be valid and not "none")
{v_2 : str} |= v_2 ≠ "none"
>>
Rule 6 (all shape dimensions of the input tensor must be positive)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 2 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0
>>
Rule 8 (output parameter must not be set to reduction operators)
{v_2 : str} |= v_2 ≠ "sum" ∧ v_2 ≠ "max" ∧ v_2 ≠ "min" ∧ v_2 ≠ "mean"
>>
Rule 9 (conditional dimension check for matrix squareness)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 2 then shape(v_1, 0) = shape(v_1, 1) else shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) = shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 2)
